Exactly 👍 — your brute force is **O(n²)**, and that’s why it times out on LeetCode.  
We need an **O(n log n) or better** solution.  

---

### 🚀 Optimal Approaches

There are a few standard ways to solve **Count of Smaller Numbers After Self**:

1. **Binary Indexed Tree (Fenwick Tree)** → O(n log n)  
2. **Segment Tree** → O(n log n)  
3. **Merge Sort with counting (Inversion count style)** → O(n log n)  
   - This is the most popular & interview-friendly method.  

---

### Merge Sort Approach (Recommended)  
Idea:  
- While merging two halves, if an element from the left is greater than an element from the right, then that left element is **bigger than all remaining elements in the right half**.  
- We accumulate counts as we merge.  

---

### C Implementation (O(n log n)):
```c
#include <stdlib.h>

typedef struct {
    int value;
    int index;
} Pair;

void merge(Pair* arr, int* counts, int left, int mid, int right, Pair* temp) {
    int i = left, j = mid + 1, k = left;
    while (i <= mid && j <= right) {
        if (arr[i].value <= arr[j].value) {
            temp[k++] = arr[j++];
        } else {
            counts[arr[i].index] += (right - j + 1);
            temp[k++] = arr[i++];
        }
    }
    while (i <= mid) temp[k++] = arr[i++];
    while (j <= right) temp[k++] = arr[j++];
    for (i = left; i <= right; i++) arr[i] = temp[i];
}

void mergeSort(Pair* arr, int* counts, int left, int right, Pair* temp) {
    if (left >= right) return;
    int mid = (left + right) / 2;
    mergeSort(arr, counts, left, mid, temp);
    mergeSort(arr, counts, mid + 1, right, temp);
    merge(arr, counts, left, mid, right, temp);
}

/**
 * Note: The returned array must be malloced, assume caller calls free().
 */
int* countSmaller(int* nums, int numsSize, int* returnSize) {
    Pair* arr = (Pair*)malloc(numsSize * sizeof(Pair));
    Pair* temp = (Pair*)malloc(numsSize * sizeof(Pair));
    int* counts = (int*)calloc(numsSize, sizeof(int));

    for (int i = 0; i < numsSize; i++) {
        arr[i].value = nums[i];
        arr[i].index = i;
    }

    mergeSort(arr, counts, 0, numsSize - 1, temp);

    *returnSize = numsSize;

    free(arr);
    free(temp);
    return counts;
}
```

---

### Complexity
- **Time:** O(n log n)  
- **Space:** O(n) (for temporary arrays and result)  

